---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
const siteUrl = Astro.site?.toString().replace(/\/$/, '') || 'https://www.arclifteq.com';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Elevated Roll-Forming Lifts & Large-Deck Platforms"
  description="Explore truck-mounted and crawler-mounted lifts for roof-panel roll formers, plus large-deck ceiling platforms. ARCLIFT supports technical selection and supply."
  ogImage="/images/equipment/elevated-roll-forming-platform.jpg"
  transparentNav={false}
>
  <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify({
    '@context': 'https://schema.org', '@type': 'Organization',
    name: 'ARCLIFT Equipment Co., Ltd.', url: siteUrl, logo: `${siteUrl}/images/logo.png`,
    description: 'Integrated equipment supplier supporting technical selection for roof-level roll forming lifts and large-deck crawler platforms.',
    contactPoint: { '@type': 'ContactPoint', telephone: '+86 15617687185', contactType: 'sales', availableLanguage: ['English', 'Chinese'] },
  })} />

  <section class="a2-hero a2-shell" aria-labelledby="hero-title">
    <div class="a2-hero-layout">
      <div class="a2-hero-title">
        <p class="a2-eyebrow">Roof-level roll-forming equipment</p>
        <h1 id="hero-title">Lift the roll former.<br />Form closer to the roof.</h1>
      </div>
      <div class="a2-hero-media" data-equipment-hero>
        <div class="a2-equipment-stage">
          <figure class="a2-equipment-main">
            <img src="/images/equipment/elevated-roll-forming-platform.jpg" width="349" height="405" alt="Extended lifting structure carrying an equipment platform above a crawler base" fetchpriority="high" />
          </figure>
          <figure class="a2-equipment-detail">
            <img src="/images/equipment/elevated-platform-detail.jpg" width="312" height="405" alt="A separate reference view of the elevated equipment platform and folding support" />
            <figcaption>Platform and support detail</figcaption>
          </figure>
        </div>
        <p class="a2-caption">Equipment reference views. Final configuration and application require review.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="a2-hero-copy">
        <p>Truck-mounted and crawler-mounted lifting equipment for roof-panel roll formers.</p>
        <div class="a2-actions">
          <a class="a2-button" href="/products/">Explore lifting systems</a>
          <a class="a2-text-link" href="#matching">What to prepare</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="a2-shell a2-identity">
    <p><strong>ARCLIFT</strong> is an integrated equipment supplier and technical selection and supply partner.</p>
    <p class="a2-identity-scope">Roof-level forming<br />Under-ceiling platforms</p>
  </div>

  <section class="a2-shell a2-section" aria-labelledby="systems-title">
    <div class="a2-section-head">
      <h2 id="systems-title">Two lifting arrangements.<br />Start with your site.</h2>
      <p>The roll former, site access and transport plan help define the equipment route.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="a2-route-grid">
      <article class="a2-route">
        <figure>
          <div class="a2-route-photo"><img src="/images/equipment/coil-handling-workflow.jpg" width="494" height="412" alt="Truck-carried lifting equipment shown handling a steel coil alongside the structure" loading="lazy" /></div>
          <figcaption class="a2-caption">Reference: truck-carried material handling, not roof-panel production.</figcaption>
        </figure>
        <h3>Truck-mounted</h3>
        <p>Bring the chassis interface, machine layout and available setup area into the same discussion.</p>
        <a class="a2-text-link" href="/products/#truck-mounted-roll-forming-lifts">Explore truck-mounted systems <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
        <p class="a2-route-input"><strong>Prepare:</strong> chassis information, machine dimensions, site layout.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="a2-route">
        <figure>
          <div class="a2-route-photo"><img class="a2-crawler-photo" src="/images/equipment/crawler-transport.jpg" width="543" height="306" alt="Folded crawler lifting equipment secured on a lowboy trailer" loading="lazy" /></div>
          <figcaption class="a2-caption">Reference: crawler equipment in transport, not an operating setup.</figcaption>
        </figure>
        <h3>Crawler-mounted</h3>
        <p>Plan the access route, support conditions and transport arrangement around the machine.</p>
        <a class="a2-text-link" href="/products/#crawler-roll-forming-lifts">Explore crawler-mounted systems <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
        <p class="a2-route-input"><strong>Prepare:</strong> access details, ground information, transport plan.</p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="a2-band" id="matching" aria-labelledby="matching-title">
    <div class="a2-shell">
      <div class="a2-section-head"><h2 id="matching-title">The lift starts with<br />the forming machine.</h2><p>Height alone is not a complete selection brief. Gather these inputs before comparing configurations.</p></div>
      <dl class="a2-inputs">
        <div><dt>Machine &amp; interface</dt><dd>Roll-former weight, dimensions and mounting arrangement.</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Outlet &amp; receiving area</dt><dd>Target outlet height, roof edge and planned panel handover.</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Site &amp; transport</dt><dd>Access, setup space, support conditions and destination.</dd></div>
      </dl>
      <a class="a2-text-link" href="/blog/high-altitude-roll-forming-lift-rfq-data/">Build a useful equipment brief <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="a2-shell a2-section a2-split" id="ceiling" aria-labelledby="ceiling-title">
    <figure class="a2-ceiling-photo">
      <img src="/images/equipment/under-ceiling-large-deck.jpg" width="611" height="452" alt="Large-deck platform positioned below the steel roof structure inside a building" loading="lazy" />
      <figcaption class="a2-caption">Under-ceiling platform reference. Main-deck and extension-zone loads need separate confirmation.</figcaption>
    </figure>
    <div class="a2-split-copy">
      <p class="a2-eyebrow">A separate product line</p>
      <h2 id="ceiling-title">More working area.<br />Beneath the ceiling.</h2>
      <p>Large-deck platforms for under-ceiling work. Review deck layout and overhead clearance separately from roof-forming equipment.</p>
      <a class="a2-text-link" href="/products/#crawler-ceiling-platforms">Explore ceiling platforms <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="a2-reading a2-shell" aria-labelledby="reading-title">
    <div class="a2-section-head"><h2 id="reading-title">Plan the interfaces,<br />not just the height.</h2><a class="a2-text-link" href="/blog/">All technical guides <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></div>
    <div class="a2-reading-links">
      <a href="/blog/crawler-vs-truck-mounted-roll-forming-system/"><span>Equipment selection</span><h3>Crawler or truck-mounted?</h3><p>Compare the route, setup and transport questions.</p><span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
      <a href="/blog/elevated-roll-forming-roof-panel-handover-zones/"><span>Roof interface</span><h3>Where does the panel go next?</h3><p>Think through the outlet, support and receiving area.</p><span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
      <a href="/blog/40hq-shipping-truck-mounted-roll-forming-lift/"><span>Delivery planning</span><h3>What needs a packing review?</h3><p>Separate a shipping concept from an approved load plan.</p><span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
    </div>
    <p class="a2-related-line">Also explore <a href="/products/#roll-forming-machines">roll-forming machine references</a> or the <a href="/compare/">equipment comparison workspace</a>.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="a2-inquiry" aria-labelledby="inquiry-title">
    <div class="a2-shell a2-inquiry-inner">
      <h2 id="inquiry-title">Tell us about<br />your roll former.</h2>
      <div><p>Planning a project or sourcing for your market? Start with the machine, the output position and the site.</p><a class="a2-button a2-button--orange" href="/contact/">Send your equipment brief</a><div class="a2-contact-links"><a href="https://wa.me/8615617687185">WhatsApp: +86 15617687185</a><a href="mailto:leelogly120@gmail.com">leelogly120@gmail.com</a></div></div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
